march/audio#audioContext.md:
The one `AudioContext` every audio source shares, made on first use; `null` where there is no Web Audio (node, old
browsers). Use it for nodes of your own that a source should hear, so everything runs in one context.

```ts
const ctx = audioContext();
if (ctx) { const osc = ctx.createOscillator(); osc.start(); const src = audioSource(osc); await src.start(); }
```

march/audio#mediaChain.md:
The audio path of an `<audio>` / `<video>` element: `{ input, output }`, made once for the element's whole life (an
element can feed only one MediaElementAudioSourceNode). By default `input → output → speakers`. Effects go between the
two: disconnect `input` from `output` and insert your nodes. Audio sources made from the element read `output`, so
meters show the processed sound. `null` without Web Audio.

```ts
const chain = mediaChain(video)!;
const eq = audioContext()!.createBiquadFilter();
chain.input.disconnect(chain.output);
chain.input.connect(eq).connect(chain.output);
```

march/audio#toAudioSource.md:
Turns a `source` prop into an AudioSource: an AudioSource is kept as it is; anything else (`"demo"`, an element, a
stream, a number function) becomes a new source that stops with the current owner. Every audio component reads its
`source` prop through it.

```ts
const src = toAudioSource(props.source);
src.use(root);
src.onUpdate(() => draw(src.level()));
```

